WEBVTT

00:00:01.090 --> 00:00:02.920
The Digital World,

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:06.040
a world inhabited by unusual 
creatures called Digimon.

00:00:06.040 --> 00:00:09.950
It has been conquered 
by the evil Bagra Army

00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:14.530
and divided into seven Kingdoms 
ruled by seven Death Generals.

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:18.310
Taiki Kudou has leapt 
into these seven Kingdoms

00:00:18.310 --> 00:00:22.020
along with his partner, 
Shoutmon, to save the Digimon.

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:25.710
This is the story of the 
friendship and adventures

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:28.540
shared by Taiki, his friends, 
and the Digimon.

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:54.390
It was an epic showdown in the 
sixth Kingdom, Canyon Land.

00:01:54.390 --> 00:01:56.930
Thanks to our newest power, X7,

00:01:56.930 --> 00:01:59.630
and Kiriha's awakening 
to his strong love,

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:03.000
we finally destroyed the Death General, 
Gravimon the Earth God.

00:02:03.000 --> 00:02:06.600
Now only the final Kingdom remains!

00:02:07.540 --> 00:02:15.630
<b>The Final Kingdom,</b>

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:15.630
<b>Bright Land of the Shining Sun</b>

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:11.220
The Final Kingdom,

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:13.620
Bright Land of the Shining Sun!

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:31.380
So this is the seventh and 
final Kingdom, Bright Land.

00:02:31.380 --> 00:02:32.630
Bright...

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:35.010
It sure does live up to its name.

00:02:35.010 --> 00:02:36.400
What beautiful light.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:39.300
We've finally made it this far.

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:42.440
Yeah. Once we get past that flag,

00:02:42.440 --> 00:02:44.320
we'll reach the Bagra Army's stronghold,

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:45.510
the Great Bagra Palace.

00:02:45.510 --> 00:02:49.580
This Kingdom is probably protected by 
the strongest of the Death Generals.

00:02:50.080 --> 00:02:51.920
Nene!

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:54.140
How do things look, Sparrowmon?

00:02:54.140 --> 00:02:55.820
Really weird!

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.220
When I go near that tower,

00:02:57.220 --> 00:02:59.090
I'm repelled by a power I can't see!

00:02:59.450 --> 00:03:01.160
We can't approach it from the air?

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:03.490
That's not all! Everyone come look!

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:17.040
This is terrible.

00:03:19.110 --> 00:03:20.870
Hey! Are you okay?

00:03:20.870 --> 00:03:22.410
We're gonna help you!

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:24.430
You can't.

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:28.500
These wedges were driven into the ground 
by the Sun Wheel General, Apollomon.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:29.950
No one can remove them.

00:03:29.950 --> 00:03:31.090
Apollomon?

00:03:32.360 --> 00:03:33.930
The Death General of this Kingdom?

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:35.680
Yes.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:37.060
Why would he do this?

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:40.680
So he can turn our pain 
into negative energy

00:03:40.680 --> 00:03:42.770
and send it to the Great Bagra Palace.

00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:45.360
I'll never forgive him!

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:47.800
I don't know if he's the 
strongest Death General or what,

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:49.910
but he's the worst King there could be!

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:52.480
You said it, Shoutmon.

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:54.250
Let's go, Taiki!

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:57.100
We've gotta destroy him 
and save this Kingdom!

00:03:58.370 --> 00:03:59.880
Insolent creatures!

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.260
I am Sethmon.

00:04:02.260 --> 00:04:03.620
I am Marsmon.

00:04:03.620 --> 00:04:04.380
Enemies?

00:04:04.380 --> 00:04:06.950
R-Run! They're the 
messengers of the tower!

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:09.730
Foolish rebels.

00:04:09.730 --> 00:04:13.970
It is inconceivable that you would 
have an audience with Lord Apollomon.

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:17.440
Come, beasts who serve our god!

00:04:20.870 --> 00:04:22.660
They've come, all right!

00:04:22.660 --> 00:04:24.340
Let's do this, guys!

00:04:24.340 --> 00:04:25.270
Right!

00:04:25.270 --> 00:04:25.980
Reload!

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:52.940
Get off!

00:04:52.940 --> 00:04:53.870
I don't think so!

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:57.580
Rock Damashi!

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:02.090
Greymon!

00:05:04.280 --> 00:05:06.020
MailBirdramon!

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:09.090
DigiXros!

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:13.260
MetalGreymon!

00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:18.000
Giga Destroyer!

00:05:26.940 --> 00:05:28.670
<i>They are used to battle.</i>

00:05:28.670 --> 00:05:31.230
<i>They make a good, well-polished team.</i>

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:35.380
<i>This may be the power that 
Lord Apollomon desires.</i>

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:38.300
Why, you...

00:05:38.710 --> 00:05:40.510
Lord Apollomon!

00:05:40.510 --> 00:05:45.160
Lord Apollomon, 
grant me the power to DigiXros!

00:05:48.820 --> 00:05:52.100
Very well, Sethmon.

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:53.870
That's Apollomon?

00:05:54.280 --> 00:05:55.870
DigiXros!

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:04.280
Sethmon Wild Mode!

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:09.770
I am the god of this Kingdom.

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:13.000
What will you do, rebels?

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:16.650
Passing yourself off as a god 
without even showing yourself?

00:06:16.650 --> 00:06:18.420
Cut the bigshot act!

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:21.460
It's burning me up!

00:06:21.460 --> 00:06:24.360
Me, too! Let's go, Shoutmon!

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:29.470
Shoutmon, Digivolve!

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:34.140
Shoutmon, Digivolve!

00:06:36.710 --> 00:06:38.970
OmegaShoutmon!

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:42.210
MetalGreymon, Digivolve!

00:06:43.810 --> 00:06:47.720
MetalGreymon, Digivolve!

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:52.560
ZekeGreymon!

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:57.340
OmegaShoutmon!

00:06:57.340 --> 00:06:58.900
ZekeGreymon!

00:06:58.900 --> 00:07:00.800
Double Xros!

00:07:03.530 --> 00:07:05.200
Double Xros!

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:10.580
Shoutmon DX!

00:07:17.010 --> 00:07:18.520
Feel my power!

00:07:24.820 --> 00:07:27.880
Behold! This is the wrath of our god!

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:29.880
Grand Heat Storm!

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:34.800
Have a look at my wrath, too!

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:36.780
Trident JusFang!

00:07:42.040 --> 00:07:43.810
Hyper Rock Magnum!

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:51.590
Th-This cannot be!

00:07:51.590 --> 00:07:54.300
Am I so helpless against them?!

00:07:55.250 --> 00:07:57.090
Enough, Sethmon.

00:08:01.160 --> 00:08:03.040
You have won.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:07.010
Very well. I shall grant 
you an audience with me.

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:10.100
Climb to the top of Apollonia Tower.

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:13.200
There's that bigshot talk again!

00:08:13.200 --> 00:08:16.470
I'll take you down in 
a heartbeat, Apollomon!

00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:18.740
We're finally about to 
meet the Death General...

00:08:18.740 --> 00:08:22.100
Marsmon, lead them.

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:22.820
Sir!

00:08:23.550 --> 00:08:25.510
Come with me.

00:08:47.710 --> 00:08:49.110
Watch your step.

00:08:49.110 --> 00:08:51.280
If you fall from here, hell awaits you.

00:08:54.480 --> 00:08:56.280
H-Hell?

00:08:56.280 --> 00:08:58.220
Stop kidding around!

00:08:58.220 --> 00:09:02.040
What's with this eternal 
staircase, anyway?

00:09:02.040 --> 00:09:03.850
Let us make haste.

00:09:04.590 --> 00:09:06.990
These stairs lead to our god.

00:09:06.990 --> 00:09:12.900
All who seek him must climb 
these stairs with their own legs.

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:15.270
So that's why I couldn't get 
close to it from the air!

00:09:15.270 --> 00:09:16.810
Yeah.

00:09:17.710 --> 00:09:19.800
Hell below if you fall, huh?

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:41.900
It's a golden flower field...

00:09:41.900 --> 00:09:45.380
Keeping a gorgeous world 
like this all to himself!

00:09:45.380 --> 00:09:46.810
I hate this guy more and more!

00:09:47.450 --> 00:09:51.960
This tower draws up life from the land 
through the cracked ground.

00:09:51.960 --> 00:09:55.340
Those wedges really are tools of a demon.

00:09:56.040 --> 00:09:57.410
Precisely.

00:10:04.570 --> 00:10:06.510
That's Apollomon?

00:10:06.510 --> 00:10:09.220
I sense incredible strength in him.

00:10:09.220 --> 00:10:13.090
To tread upon the weak and 
feed upon their tears...

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:15.160
That is the Bagra Army's way.

00:10:15.570 --> 00:10:18.700
If you realize that, 
we can get right to the point!

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:22.490
You heroes have come through 
such abhorrent Kingdoms

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:25.270
and found your way here.

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:27.210
Taiki Kudou,

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:28.580
Nene Amano,

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:30.010
Kiriha Aonuma,

00:10:30.010 --> 00:10:33.770
and your Digimon companions.

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:37.800
Splendid. I have awaited your arrival.

00:10:38.480 --> 00:10:41.030
I must be forward with you now.

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:44.100
I am, in truth...

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:46.830
a Digimon on the side of justice.

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:55.630
You're a Digimon of justice?!

00:10:56.440 --> 00:10:58.420
Please, fight by my side,

00:10:58.420 --> 00:11:00.620
so that we may defeat Bagramon

00:11:00.620 --> 00:11:02.960
and halt the approach of D5,

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:05.610
the Day of Ultimate Destruction.

00:11:25.300 --> 00:11:28.870
So, are you saying you've been 
pretending to be a bad guy?

00:11:28.870 --> 00:11:32.910
I am by nature a Digimon 
with a just heart.

00:11:32.910 --> 00:11:35.180
Even after the Digital 
World was conquered

00:11:35.180 --> 00:11:37.360
and I was made a Death General,

00:11:37.360 --> 00:11:40.710
I have concealed this truth and 
never once lost sight of it.

00:11:40.710 --> 00:11:43.860
No matter how much power I possess,

00:11:43.860 --> 00:11:46.200
I cannot defeat Bagramon alone.

00:11:46.770 --> 00:11:50.920
I believed that a hero would one 
day appear to fight by my side.

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:55.040
You, who have come through 
each of the Kingdoms,

00:11:55.040 --> 00:11:57.700
are the ones I have been waiting for.

00:11:57.700 --> 00:11:59.100
Wait a minute!

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:00.890
What's with the horrible 
things you're doing

00:12:00.890 --> 00:12:02.100
to this Kingdom's Digimon, then?

00:12:02.500 --> 00:12:05.380
All to deceive Bagramon.

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:07.900
Also, in doing what I've done,

00:12:07.900 --> 00:12:10.540
I have at least allowed them to live.

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:13.580
I realize that it is a terrible sin.

00:12:14.770 --> 00:12:16.250
What do you think, Taiki?

00:12:17.480 --> 00:12:19.970
He doesn't seem to be lying.

00:12:21.490 --> 00:12:23.860
And how do you plan to defeat Bagramon?

00:12:23.860 --> 00:12:28.090
First, I would require you to act 
as though I had defeated you.

00:12:28.090 --> 00:12:29.230
What?!

00:12:29.230 --> 00:12:31.950
Then I will have an 
audience with Bagramon

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:34.270
and destroy the Great 
Bagra Palace from within.

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:40.070
I wouldn't put it past you to defeat 
us for real after telling us that.

00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:42.280
If you truly are just,

00:12:42.280 --> 00:12:44.610
you should just let us defeat you.

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:45.800
You are right.

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:48.650
However, our opponent 
possesses enormous power.

00:12:48.650 --> 00:12:52.980
If you encounter trouble in battle before 
reaching the Great Bagra Palace,

00:12:52.980 --> 00:12:54.450
we will be out of time.

00:12:54.450 --> 00:12:55.620
Out of time?

00:12:56.710 --> 00:13:00.090
When the Code Crown is filled 
with negative energy,

00:13:01.030 --> 00:13:04.370
the day of destruction of 
all worlds will come.

00:13:04.860 --> 00:13:07.560
That is what they call D5.

00:13:08.330 --> 00:13:10.130
There is no more time.

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:14.150
Please, cooperate with me.

00:13:16.170 --> 00:13:18.590
What do we do, Taiki?

00:13:29.790 --> 00:13:32.790
Apollomon, give me a little bit of time.

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:34.520
I want to talk with my friends.

00:13:34.520 --> 00:13:35.960
All right.

00:13:42.130 --> 00:13:45.100
Kiriha, let's help Apollomon.

00:13:45.100 --> 00:13:46.120
No, thanks.

00:13:46.120 --> 00:13:46.600
Kiriha...

00:13:46.600 --> 00:13:49.460
I want to take back the Code Crown

00:13:49.460 --> 00:13:52.070
so I can bring Deckerdramon 
back to life.

00:13:52.070 --> 00:13:54.980
That's why I have to defeat 
all the Death Generals.

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:56.280
No exceptions.

00:13:56.280 --> 00:13:59.120
But Apollomon isn't lying.

00:13:59.120 --> 00:14:01.620
It's just my intuition, but...

00:14:03.280 --> 00:14:05.080
What do you think, Nene?

00:14:05.080 --> 00:14:08.270
If Apollomon helps us,

00:14:08.270 --> 00:14:09.780
I think it would give us a chance.

00:14:09.780 --> 00:14:14.660
If the plans for D5 are true, 
all the more reason.

00:14:14.660 --> 00:14:15.620
But...

00:14:15.620 --> 00:14:16.590
But?

00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:21.510
Nene's the same as me. 
She doesn't buy his story.

00:14:21.940 --> 00:14:23.960
It's two to one, Taiki.

00:14:32.080 --> 00:14:34.800
Just telling them to believe 
me would never work...

00:14:40.430 --> 00:14:42.150
It's no good!

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:46.740
Looks like we'll have to force 
our way in and climb up, Sir Yuu!

00:14:46.740 --> 00:14:48.630
Let's wait a little longer.

00:14:49.080 --> 00:14:50.850
Oh, here they come!

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:02.780
Have you made a decision?

00:15:02.780 --> 00:15:04.620
This is our decision.

00:15:05.250 --> 00:15:06.350
Kiriha! Nene!

00:15:06.350 --> 00:15:07.230
Wait!

00:15:14.630 --> 00:15:15.440
Apollomon!

00:15:16.070 --> 00:15:18.520
It is no matter, Taiki Kudou.

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:22.350
I need only endure until 
they choose to believe me.

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:26.070
H-He might just be a 
good guy after all...

00:15:26.070 --> 00:15:27.410
Shoutmon, let's stop them!

00:15:27.410 --> 00:15:28.510
Right!

00:15:28.510 --> 00:15:29.680
Shoutmon!

00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:30.890
Ballistamon!

00:15:30.890 --> 00:15:32.050
Dorulumon!

00:15:32.050 --> 00:15:33.270
Starmons!

00:15:33.270 --> 00:15:34.790
DigiXros!

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:37.020
DigiXros!

00:15:55.670 --> 00:15:58.590
Shoutmon X4!

00:16:02.660 --> 00:16:03.840
What are you doing?!

00:16:04.150 --> 00:16:06.210
Chill out, old man MetalGreymon!

00:16:06.210 --> 00:16:08.010
I am calm!

00:16:08.010 --> 00:16:10.850
What Kiriha says is not wrong!

00:16:10.850 --> 00:16:13.150
I know that, but still!

00:16:14.390 --> 00:16:15.400
Hey!

00:16:15.400 --> 00:16:17.790
You're the one who needs to chill out!

00:16:17.790 --> 00:16:19.290
Kiriha, stop!

00:16:19.290 --> 00:16:22.490
I told you, you have to get rid 
of those naive ideas, Taiki!

00:16:25.460 --> 00:16:27.430
Let go of me, X4!

00:16:28.520 --> 00:16:30.470
Lay off already!

00:16:30.470 --> 00:16:33.120
Giga Destroyer!

00:16:36.610 --> 00:16:37.280
Taiki!

00:17:00.010 --> 00:17:02.630
You saved me, Apollomon.

00:17:02.630 --> 00:17:04.070
Are you okay, Taiki?

00:17:04.070 --> 00:17:06.300
Yeah, I'm okay.

00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:13.210
What are those cuts?

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:16.930
Merely a small atonement.

00:17:16.930 --> 00:17:20.920
With each Digimon I punish, 
I inflict a wound upon myself

00:17:21.230 --> 00:17:23.350
to deplete my own power.

00:17:24.300 --> 00:17:28.360
By now, my right arm is nearly immobile.

00:17:28.360 --> 00:17:32.070
I do not believe such an act 
will clear me of my sin...

00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:36.100
But I could not stand by and do nothing.

00:17:36.650 --> 00:17:39.650
Apollomon... You really are...

00:17:40.100 --> 00:17:42.320
What a noble Digimon...

00:17:44.140 --> 00:17:46.460
All right. We'll trust you.

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:50.350
Not your justice, 
but your nobility and pride.

00:17:50.810 --> 00:17:51.880
Kiriha...

00:17:51.880 --> 00:17:53.570
Yay!

00:17:53.570 --> 00:17:55.270
Thanks, Kiriha!

00:17:55.270 --> 00:17:58.510
Get off me, you weirdo!

00:17:58.510 --> 00:17:59.790
Thank you.

00:18:11.340 --> 00:18:13.530
Negligence is a big enemy.

00:18:13.530 --> 00:18:14.810
A big enemy, indeed.

00:18:14.810 --> 00:18:15.470
Yuu!

00:18:15.470 --> 00:18:17.280
Tuwarmon, you...

00:18:17.280 --> 00:18:19.720
No! Why are you here?

00:18:19.720 --> 00:18:22.370
Even if you possess the 
power of DarkKnightmon,

00:18:22.370 --> 00:18:25.480
you should not be able to interfere 
in the top floor of this tower!

00:18:25.480 --> 00:18:31.260
We're here because you 
invited us, Apollomon.

00:18:31.260 --> 00:18:32.550
I did?

00:18:33.400 --> 00:18:34.590
What are you saying?

00:18:34.590 --> 00:18:36.810
Oh, I forgot.

00:18:36.810 --> 00:18:39.870
The bright you doesn't know about that.

00:18:39.870 --> 00:18:43.000
You defeated your subordinate 
Marsmon yourself, too.

00:18:43.000 --> 00:18:44.260
What?

00:18:44.260 --> 00:18:47.110
It's true, partner.

00:18:47.110 --> 00:18:51.340
I have been inside you 
for a long, long time.

00:18:54.110 --> 00:18:55.980
What is this sensation?!

00:18:55.980 --> 00:18:56.950
Apollomon!

00:19:14.670 --> 00:19:20.200
I am the evil dark spot that 
sleeps within the brilliant sun,

00:19:20.200 --> 00:19:21.610
Whispered.

00:19:21.930 --> 00:19:22.840
Whispered?

00:19:23.290 --> 00:19:26.800
Another program sleeping inside you.

00:19:26.800 --> 00:19:31.250
Lord Bagramon and DarkKnightmon 
installed it in you as a precaution.

00:19:31.740 --> 00:19:34.460
If it became necessary, 
it could overtake your consciousness

00:19:34.460 --> 00:19:37.620
and make you act as a soldier of evil.

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:41.550
I know you've been plotting 
a rebellion in secret,

00:19:41.550 --> 00:19:44.100
but the truth is that you were 
the one to betray yourself.

00:19:44.650 --> 00:19:45.830
That's a lie!

00:19:48.400 --> 00:19:50.130
It's no lie.

00:19:50.560 --> 00:19:52.710
I'm going to take over now.

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:55.370
I'll take care of 
annihilating the brats.

00:19:58.140 --> 00:19:58.880
Apollomon!

00:19:59.450 --> 00:20:00.950
Taiki Kudou!

00:20:00.950 --> 00:20:02.610
Don't lose! Hang in there!

00:20:03.130 --> 00:20:04.340
I'm sorry.

00:20:04.340 --> 00:20:07.480
I never thought this would happen.

00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:10.050
Perhaps Kiriha and Nene were 
correct in doubting me.

00:20:10.050 --> 00:20:10.990
Apollomon!

00:20:11.740 --> 00:20:13.310
Now that it's come to this,

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:16.570
you must be the ones 
to... the ones to...

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:22.700
Apollomon!

00:20:34.120 --> 00:20:35.470
Now, then...

00:20:35.470 --> 00:20:38.510
I'll help you out, Tuwarmon.

00:20:38.510 --> 00:20:40.630
Arrow of Whispered!

00:20:45.360 --> 00:20:47.930
Whispered, time to start the game.

00:20:47.930 --> 00:20:48.690
Yes.

00:20:55.120 --> 00:20:56.470
No! If we don't stop this...

00:20:56.880 --> 00:20:58.310
We need X7!

00:20:58.310 --> 00:21:00.940
It's our only chance to 
get out of this and fight!

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:04.440
<i>But if we defeat Whispered with X7,</i>

00:21:04.440 --> 00:21:05.810
<i>Apollomon will...</i>

00:21:05.810 --> 00:21:08.210
We're using X7!

00:21:08.210 --> 00:21:09.120
Yeah!

00:21:09.120 --> 00:21:10.980
Let's do it!

00:21:10.980 --> 00:21:12.990
Great Xros!

00:21:17.060 --> 00:21:19.260
Taiki, what are you doing?!

00:21:19.260 --> 00:21:20.670
Taiki?

00:21:21.860 --> 00:21:24.560
Shoutmon! Digivolve!

00:21:26.110 --> 00:21:27.470
Huh?

00:21:27.470 --> 00:21:28.850
I'm not Digivolving!

00:21:29.620 --> 00:21:31.320
I just can't...

00:21:31.320 --> 00:21:32.990
Taiki! What are you doing?!

00:21:37.310 --> 00:21:40.040
O-Oh, crap! Maybe this really does...

00:21:40.040 --> 00:21:41.330
...lead to hell, Brother!

00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:45.350
<i>No! This is... This is my fault!</i>

00:21:53.360 --> 00:21:54.720
All right!

00:21:54.720 --> 00:21:56.820
Now for the last stage,

00:21:56.820 --> 00:21:58.000
and my turn!

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:02.370
Let's enjoy the fight with Taiki 
and his friends, Whispered.

00:22:02.720 --> 00:22:06.120
Yes, let's.

00:22:07.720 --> 00:22:09.690
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:22:09.690 --> 00:22:13.200
<b>Digimon Data Collection</b>

00:22:10.530 --> 00:22:13.200
Digimon Data Collection!

00:22:13.230 --> 00:22:17.160
<b>Listen to the Digimon's melody!</b>

00:22:13.730 --> 00:22:17.160
Listen to the melody of 
this Digimon I caught!

00:22:14.160 --> 00:22:15.160
<b>Melody starts in 3 seconds.</b>

00:22:15.160 --> 00:22:16.160
<b>Melody starts in 2 seconds.</b>

00:22:16.160 --> 00:22:17.160
<b>Melody starts in 1 second.</b>

